HST Office: in Writer, Backspace with a whole table selected (Ctrl+A twice in a cell, or a cell
selection covering every cell) deletes the table, as in Word; before it only cleared the cells
and deleting a table needed Table > Delete > Table. The table goes through the same core call as
that command (one undo step, same change tracking, cursor after the table or else before it).
Delete still clears the cells; partial selections, read-only or protected cells, DDE tables and
tables already deleted in tracked changes keep the old Backspace. With nested tables the table
the selected cells belong to is deleted. Logic in sw/source/uibase/hst/selectedtabledelete.cxx;
the hook is the .uno:SwBackspace slot in sw/source/uibase/shells/basesh.cxx.

